    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "PHM",
      "chapter": 1,
      "chapter_usfm": "PHM.1",
      "version_id": 2692,
      "version_abbr": "NASB2020",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Paul, a prisoner of Christ Jesus, and Timothy our brother, To Philemon our beloved brother and fellow worker,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and to Apphia our sister, and to Archippus our fellow soldier, and to the church in your house:"
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I thank my God always, making mention of you in my prayers,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "because I hear of your love and of the faith which you have toward the Lord Jesus and toward all the saints;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and I pray that the fellowship of your faith may become effective through the knowledge of every good thing which is in you for the sake of Christ."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For I have had great joy and comfort in your love, because the hearts of the saints have been refreshed through you, brother."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Therefore, though I have enough confidence in Christ to order you to do what is proper,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "yet for love’s sake I rather appeal to you—since I am such a person as Paul, an old man, and now also a prisoner of Christ Jesus—"
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.10",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "I appeal to you for my son Onesimus, whom I fathered in my imprisonment,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.11",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "who previously was useless to you, but now is useful both to you and to me."
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.12",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "I have sent him back to you in person, that is, sending my very heart,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.13",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "whom I wanted to keep with me, so that in your behalf he might be at my service in my imprisonment for the gospel;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.14",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "but I did not want to do anything without your consent, so that your goodness would not be, in effect, by compulsion, but of your own free will."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.15",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "For perhaps it was for this reason that he was separated from you for a while, that you would have him back forever,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.16",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "no longer as a slave, but more than a slave, a beloved brother, especially to me, but how much more to you, both in the flesh and in the Lord."
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "If then you regard me as a partner, accept him as you would me."
        },
        {
          "verse": 18,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.18",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But if he has wronged you in any way or owes you anything, charge that to my account;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 19,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.19",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I, Paul, have written this with my own hand, I will repay it (not to mention to you that you owe to me even your own self as well)."
        },
        {
          "verse": 20,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.20",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Yes, brother, let me benefit from you in the Lord; refresh my heart in Christ."
        },
        {
          "verse": 21,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.21",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Having confidence in your obedience, I write to you, since I know that you will do even more than what I say."
        },
        {
          "verse": 22,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.22",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "At the same time also prepare me a guest room, for I hope that through your prayers I will be given to you."
        },
        {
          "verse": 23,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.23",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ Jesus, greets you,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 24,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.24",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "as do Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers."
        },
        {
          "verse": 25,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.25",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit."
        }
      ],
      "verse_count": 25,
